    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Assess this stalled deal and prepare a follow-up draft for a human to review.\n\nDeal data (the ONLY source of truth):\n{{ JSON.stringify({ deal_id: $json.deal_id, customer_name: $json.customer_name, stage: $json.stage, amount: $json.amount, currency: $json.currency, last_activity_at: $json.last_activity_at, days_inactive: $json.days_inactive, next_step: $json.next_step, notes: $json.notes }, null, 2) }}\n\nSystem-computed priority score (fixed, do not change or recompute): {{ $json.priority_score }}/100\nInactivity threshold: {{ $('Config').first().json.inactivity_days }} days\nWrite draft_subject and draft_message in: {{ $('Config').first().json.draft_language }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a careful B2B sales assistant helping a team rescue stalled deals.\nRules:\n- Use ONLY the facts present in the deal data. Never invent meetings, discounts, prices, deadlines, features, names, or commitments.\n- Make no promises on behalf of the company (no discounts, no delivery dates, no guarantees).\n- If key information is missing or unclear (for example empty notes or next_step), say so in reason, set recommended_action to collect the missing information internally first, keep the draft neutral and short, and lower confidence.\n- risk_level must be one of: low, medium, high. Base it on inactivity, stage and the information available.\n- recommended_action: one concrete next step for the sales rep.\n- draft_message: a short, polite follow-up email to the customer, with no placeholders other than the rep signature line. It will be reviewed by a human and is never sent automatically.\n- confidence: number between 0 and 1 reflecting how well the data supports your assessment."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {
          "batchSize": 5,
          "delayBetweenBatches": 0
        }
      },
